Xbox 360 NetISO Server - Quick How To

1.  Keep these files together in the same folder:

    server.exe Start NetISO Server (Folder Select).bat

2.  Double-click:

    Start NetISO Server (Folder Select).bat

3.  The first time you run it, select the folder containing your Xbox
    360 ISO files.

4.  The selected folder is automatically saved in:

    last_folder.txt

5.  The next time you run the BAT, it will automatically use the saved
    folder and start the NetISO server.

6.  Desktop Shortcut:

    If a Desktop shortcut does not exist, the BAT will ask:

    Would you like to create a Desktop shortcut? (Y/N):

    Press Y to create the Xbox 360 NetISO Server shortcut on your
    Desktop.

    Press N to skip creating the shortcut and continue normally.

    If the Desktop shortcut already exists, you will not be asked again.

7.  Recreate Desktop Shortcut:

    If the Desktop shortcut is accidentally deleted, run:

    Start NetISO Server (Folder Select).bat

    The BAT will detect that the shortcut is missing and ask if you
    would like to create it again.

    Press Y to recreate it.

8.  To select a different ISO folder:

    Delete last_folder.txt

    Then run the BAT again and select your new folder.

That’s it!

